The claim 'Healthy habits, *in a certain way*, can protect your brain as you age.' is supported by the citation.
<accept> The article explicitly states that a "positive impact of lifestyle interventions on cognition (brain function) in older adults as a preventive measure" and that "a healthy lifestyle may provide a cognitive reserve to maintain brain function independent of Alzheimer’s disease and other common neuropathologies of dementia." It also mentions that "These five lifestyle factors may support prevention of dementia and resilience to Alzheimer’s and other brain diseases." These statements directly support the idea that healthy habits can protect the brain as one ages. </accept>

